<title>GERMANY: West German August adjusted unemployment rises.</title>
<headline>West German August adjusted unemployment rises.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Aug 96	  Jul 96	   Aug 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    2.779 million     2.765 million	2.543 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		2.806 million     2.780 million	2.580 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +26,000	 +9,000	    n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		9.0 pct	 9.0 pct	  8.2 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	116,474	 179,490	  62,478</p>
<p> Vacancies		   274,150	 291,681	  277,078</p>
<p> Change in number in wrk Jun 96	  May 96</p>
<p>				 -5,000	  -16,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets. Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today. ---Bonn Newsroom 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
